<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Android launch window, i.e. what is on screen between the launcher tap and Flutter's
  first frame.

  IT IS A SINGLE COLOUR ON PURPOSE, AND THAT COLOUR IS THE DESIGN'S GROUND. Flutter's first
  frame is the splash screen, which paints #0B0D0F, so anything else here is a flash. There
  was one: this file used to be a <layer-list> holding @android:color/white, and the
  drawable-v21/ copy that actually won on every supported device held
  ?android:colorBackground, which resolves to WHITE under LaunchTheme's Theme.Light parent.
  A light-mode phone opened Nivora with a white rectangle that snapped to near-black.

  The -v21 variant is deleted rather than fixed: it only existed because ?android: attributes
  needed API 21, and minSdk has been above that for years, so it was the live file and this
  one was dead. One file now, correct on every API level.

  A <color> root rather than a <layer-list> also matters on Android 12+, where the system
  splash screen adopts windowBackground when — and only when — it is a single colour. A
  layer-list falls back to the theme's colorBackground, which is the white this removes.

  If a logo is ever added here it must be a <layer-list> again, and windowSplashScreenBackground
  must then be set explicitly in values-v31/ to keep Android 12 from falling back to white.
-->
<color xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:color="@color/nivora_ground" />
